From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: account for PPPoE session header in PPE MTU

A PPPoE session adds PPPOE_SES_HLEN (8 bytes) between the Ethernet
header and the IP payload. The PPE FP_EGRESS_MTU register and the
WAN_MTU0 register are compared against the on-wire L2 frame length,
so a PPPoE uplink that does not budget those 8 bytes silently drops
full-size frames: a 1492-byte PPPoE payload produces a 1500+8+VLAN
byte L2 frame that exceeds the programmed limit.

Add the PPPoE session header on the uplink GDM devices only. In
airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size() the MTU is aggregated across every
device sharing the QDMA/port, so the check happens per-device inside
the aggregation loop: an uplink GDM contributes
mtu + VLAN_ETH_HLEN + PPPOE_SES_HLEN, while a LAN port keeps the
VLAN-only accounting and is not given eight bytes of needless
headroom.

Ported from naoki66's XR1710G tree (920-17). Adapted: the original
gates the extra headroom on AIROHA_DEV_F_PON, a flag introduced by
the AN7581 PON series not present in this tree. This tree instead
reserves the PPPoE headroom on every uplink (non-LAN) GDM, which
covers PPPoE on the regular WAN port as well as on a PON uplink; the
registers are max-length checks, so the extra 8 bytes on a
non-PPPoE uplink is harmless.

Source: https://github.com/naoki66/ImmortalWrt-for-Gemtek-brightspeed
Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 10 +++++++---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <net/pkt_cls.h>
 #include <net/tcp.h>
 #include <uapi/linux/ppp_defs.h>
+#include <linux/if_pppox.h>

 #include "airoha_regs.h"
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
@@ -2626,11 +2627,18 @@ static void airoha_dev_set_xmit_frame_si
 {
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = netdev_priv(netdev);

 	airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size(dev);
+	/* A PPPoE session can only egress through an uplink GDM; its 8-byte
+	 * session header (PPPOE_SES_HLEN) sits between the Ethernet header and
+	 * the IP payload, so it counts into the L2 frame length the WAN MTU
+	 * register is compared against, on top of the operator VLAN tag that
+	 * VLAN_ETH_HLEN already covers. LAN ports stay VLAN-only.
+	 */
 	if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
 		airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0, WAN_MTU0_MASK,
 			      FIELD_PREP(WAN_MTU0_MASK,
-					 VLAN_ETH_HLEN + netdev->mtu));
+					 VLAN_ETH_HLEN + PPPOE_SES_HLEN +
+					 netdev->mtu));
 }

 static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_device *netdev)
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -171,6 +172,7 @@ void airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size(stru
 		struct airoha_gdm_dev *d = port->devs[i];
 		struct net_device *netdev;
 		struct airoha_qdma *q;
+		u32 mtu;

 		if (!d)
 			continue;
@@ -180,10 +182,21 @@ void airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size(stru
 			continue;

 		netdev = netdev_from_priv(d);
-		if (netif_running(netdev))
-			len = max_t(u32, len, netdev->mtu);
+		if (!netif_running(netdev))
+			continue;
+
+		/* The register is compared against the on-wire L2 length, so
+		 * every encapsulation on this egress path has to be added to
+		 * the aggregated MTU. VLAN_ETH_HLEN applies to all ports; an
+		 * uplink GDM can additionally carry a PPPoE session whose
+		 * PPPOE_SES_HLEN sits between Ethernet and the IP payload.
+		 */
+		mtu = netdev->mtu + VLAN_ETH_HLEN;
+		if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(d))
+			mtu += 8; /* PPPOE_SES_HLEN, no if_pppox.h include */
+
+		len = max_t(u32, len, mtu);
 	}
-	len += VLAN_ETH_HLEN;

 	ppe_id = !airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) && airoha_ppe_is_enabled(eth, 1);
 	index = port->id == AIROHA_GDM4_IDX ? 7 : port->id;
